# 7. AGENT ORCHESTRATION AND TASK MANAGEMENT

## 7.1 Task Lifecycle

Every Agent task must follow a persistent lifecycle:

1. Created.
2. Assigned.
3. In Progress.
4. Awaiting Input.
5. Awaiting Approval.
6. Approved.
7. Rejected.
8. Completed.
9. Failed.
10. Cancelled.

Not every task requires approval.

Internal research and drafting tasks can complete without approval.

Any task that initiates an external action must enter Awaiting Approval.

## 7.2 Task Object

Every task must contain:

- Task ID.
- Business ID.
- Task title.
- Task description.
- Assigned Agent.
- Priority.
- Status.
- Input data.
- Output data.
- Related entity.
- Creation date.
- Start date.
- Completion date.
- Error details.
- Estimated AI cost.
- Approval requirement.

## 7.3 Agent Execution Rules

- Agents must only use authorized tools.
- Agents must not execute arbitrary code.
- Agents must not access other users' data.
- Agents must not expose secrets.
- Agents must respect rate limits.
- Agent outputs must be validated before saving.
- Failed tasks must be logged.
- Retry operations must be controlled.
- The same external action must not execute twice because of retries.

## 7.4 Approval Workflow

Each approval request must include:

- Requested action.
- Agent requesting approval.
- Exact content or payload.
- Target platform or recipient.
- Related business object.
- Relevant parameters.
- Request creation time.
- Approval status.

Available actions:

- Approve.
- Reject.
- Edit and Request New Approval.

After approval:
- Record the owner's identity.
- Record the approved payload.
- Record the approval timestamp.
- Execute only the approved payload.
- Save the execution result.

If the execution fails, show Failed status rather than claiming success.

